'''Genma Saotome (Panda)''' is an [[:Category:Super Rare Cats|Super Rare Cat]] that can be obtained by playing the [[Cat Capsule#Rare Capsule|Rare Capsule]] during [[Ranma 1/2 Collaboration Event]]. He was added in [[Version 11.7 Update|Version 11.7]].

{{Cat Info
|ID = 672
|rarity = SR
|name1 = Genma Saotome (Panda)
|name2 = Genma Saotome
}}

==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Genma Saotome''' at level 10.

==Strategy/Usage==
Genma Saotome can be best described as an [[:Category:Anti-Traitless Cats|anti-Traitless]]/[[:Category:Anti-Aku Cats|Aku]] [[Weightlifter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Pizza Cat]]. Against Traitless, he can be used against the likes of [[R.Ost]], [[Wild Doge]], [[Wall Doge]], [[Otta-smack-u]], [[Dagshund]], [[Dolphina]] and so much more. However, Traitless foes have a wide variety of ranges, and he tends to struggle against midrange/backline enemies such as [[Rain D.]], [[Le'boin]], [[THE SLOTH]] due to his short range.

Against Aku however, he has fewer viable targets, as many Aku have [[Shield]]s that could reduce his effectiveness, although his Massive Damage allows him to break Shields with brute force. Additionally, his lack of immunity to [[Surge Attack]]s means that [[:Category:Death Surge Enemies|Death Surge Enemies]] could easily destroy him.

Overall, compared to Pizza Cat against his target trait, he has higher range and is cheaper, and both moves and attacks faster. However, Pizza Cat is better within his niche due to his [[Talents]], higher survivability and full backswing attack with shorter foreswing.

{{Job|Classification = Nuker & Midranger}}

